{
  "name": "AI Error Digest – Daily Failure Summary",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Sticky Note – Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-1100, -60],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 460,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## 🤖 AI Error Digest\n\nInstead of a push for every single failure, get **one** calm, readable summary once a day: what failed, how often, and what to look at first — written by an LLM.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Runs once a day (default 08:00).\n2. Pulls the last 24 h of `error` executions from the n8n API.\n3. Aggregates them by workflow.\n4. An LLM turns the raw counts into a prioritized, plain-language digest.\n5. Delivers it as a single message on your channel of choice.\n\n**Setup:**\n1. Set `N8N_BASE_URL` and `LOOKBACK_HOURS` in the **Config** node.\n2. Add an **n8n API key** as a *Header Auth* credential (Name `X-N8N-API-KEY`) on the HTTP Request node.\n3. Add your LLM credential to the **Chat Model** node (OpenAI by default — swap for Anthropic, Google, Ollama, etc.).\n4. Pick a delivery channel on the right.\n5. **Activate** the workflow.\n\n*No failures in the window → a short \"all clear\" branch runs instead (disabled by default).*"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-model",
      "name": "Sticky Note – Model",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [200, 280],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 300,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## 🧠 Swap the model freely\n\nThe **Chat Model** sub-node is OpenAI by default. Replace it with any chat model node (Anthropic, Google Gemini, Ollama, Groq…) — just connect the new model to the *Summarize Errors* chain. The prompt stays the same."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-delivery",
      "name": "Sticky Note – Delivery Channels",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [900, -280],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 400,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "## 📣 Daily digest — pick your channel(s)\n\n**Slack** is enabled by default. To use another channel, enable it and disable Slack:\n\n- **Telegram** — set your chat ID\n- **Email** — set from/to addresses\n- **WorkflowBuddy** — native iOS push, see the note below ⬇️"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-workflowbuddy",
      "name": "Sticky Note – WorkflowBuddy",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [900, 340],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 360,
        "color": 4,
        "content": "## 📱 WorkflowBuddy (iOS push)\n\nGet the daily digest as a native push notification on your iPhone — no Slack or Telegram needed.\n\n1. Install [**Workflow Buddy**](https://apps.apple.com/app/id6760253861) from the App Store.\n2. In the app, open **Settings → Push API** and copy your key.\n3. In n8n, create a **Header Auth** credential:\n   - Name: `Authorization`\n   - Value: `Bearer wb_…` (your key)\n4. Select the credential in this node and enable it.\n\n*Free tier currently includes 50 pushes/day. The digest is one message; keep it concise (≤1000 chars).*"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-schedule",
      "name": "Every Day at 08:00",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [-580, -60],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "days",
              "daysInterval": 1,
              "triggerAtHour": 8
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-config",
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [-360, -60],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "N8N_BASE_URL",
              "value": "https://n8n.example.com",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "LOOKBACK_HOURS",
              "value": 24,
              "type": "number"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-list-errors",
      "name": "List Failed Executions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [-140, -60],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $json.N8N_BASE_URL }}/api/v1/executions",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "status",
              "value": "error"
            },
            {
              "name": "limit",
              "value": "100"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-aggregate",
      "name": "Aggregate Errors",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [120, -60],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Group the last LOOKBACK_HOURS of error executions by workflow.\nconst cfg = $('Config').first().json;\nconst lookbackHours = cfg.LOOKBACK_HOURS ?? 24;\nconst cutoff = Date.now() - lookbackHours * 3_600_000;\n\nconst body = $input.first().json;\nconst execs = (body.data || []).filter((e) => {\n  const t = new Date(e.startedAt || e.stoppedAt || 0).getTime();\n  return t >= cutoff;\n});\n\nconst groups = {};\nfor (const e of execs) {\n  const name = e.workflowData?.name ?? `workflow ${e.workflowId ?? '?'}`;\n  groups[name] = (groups[name] ?? 0) + 1;\n}\n\nconst total = execs.length;\nconst lines = Object.entries(groups)\n  .sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1])\n  .map(([name, count]) => `- ${name}: ${count} failure(s)`);\n\nconst errorReport =\n  total === 0\n    ? `No failed executions in the last ${lookbackHours}h.`\n    : `Total failed executions in the last ${lookbackHours}h: ${total}\\nBy workflow (most failures first):\\n${lines.join('\\n')}`;\n\nreturn [{ json: { hasErrors: total > 0, total, lookbackHours, errorReport } }];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-if-errors",
      "name": "Any Errors?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [380, -60],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.hasErrors }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-chat-model",
      "name": "Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [420, 160],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-4o-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-summarize",
      "name": "Summarize Errors",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
      "position": [620, -60],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an SRE assistant. Write a short daily error digest for an n8n operator based on the data below. Be concise (max ~600 characters), plain language, no markdown headers. Lead with the single most important thing to check first, then list the rest briefly. If counts are high, say so plainly.\n\nData:\n{{ $json.errorReport }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-format",
      "name": "Build Digest Message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [880, -60],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "f1",
              "name": "digest",
              "value": "={{ $json.text.slice(0, 1000) }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-alert-slack",
      "name": "Send: Slack",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [1180, -180],
      "parameters": {
        "select": "channel",
        "channelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "#alerts"
        },
        "text": "=📋 *Daily n8n error digest*\n{{ $json.digest }}",
        "otherOptions": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-alert-telegram",
      "name": "Send: Telegram",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [1180, 0],
      "disabled": true,
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "YOUR_CHAT_ID",
        "text": "=📋 Daily n8n error digest\n{{ $json.digest }}",
        "additionalFields": {}
